# LLM-GC's own credential. Copy this file to .env (git-ignored) and fill in one of the first
# two lines. `llm-gc` reads .env from the folder you start it in; a blank line counts as not set.
#
# It pays only for LLM-GC's own short calls: summarising old exchanges and reading their facts.
# Your conversation still uses your client's own login (Claude Code's, for one), which LLM-GC
# passes on and never stores.

# An Anthropic API key from console.anthropic.com, billed to that Console account (a Claude Pro
# or Max subscription does not include one), or a key your company's gateway accepts.
# Sent as x-api-key.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Or a bearer token, sent as Authorization: what a company gateway often takes instead of a
# key. Either or both; each is sent when set.
ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=

# Only when LLM-GC summarises with OpenAI (`provider = "openai"` under [summary]).
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Every other setting belongs in llm-gc.toml, which `llm-gc config init` writes. Any of them
# can also be set here as LLM_GC_<NAME>, such as LLM_GC_LOG_LEVEL=DEBUG: see Configuration in
# the README.
